2,Meskwaki Tribe: Daily Life Songs | Iowa PBS,https://www.iowapbs.org/education/findiowa/media/9503/meskwaki-tribe-daily-life-songs,"(Meskwaki tribal members dancing a traditional dance.) [Stephanie Snow] The songs were basically like everyday social songs [Abby Brown] Okay. [Stephanie] Lullabies, love songs that could be done on flute as well, hunting and gathering songs. [Abby] Also cause for celebration. [Stephanie] Right. [Abby] Okay. [Stephanie] But these songs are meant to sort of. . . Some of them are obviously ...",Meskwaki,Algic
3,Meskwaki Tribe: Daily Life Songs | Iowa PBS,https://www.iowapbs.org/education/resources/link/10308/meskwaki-tribe-daily-life-songs,Meskwaki Tribe: Daily Life Songs Songs are passed down from generation to generation for a variety of different reasons. Let's learn more,Meskwaki,Algic
4,Meskwaki Nation YouTube Videos & Livestream of Tribal Events,https://www.meskwaki.org/video-gallery/,"Click to gain access to the Meskwaki's Youtube channel or our livestreaming of events. We stream events for the Settlement School, the annual powwow & more.",Meskwaki,Algic
5,Meskwaki Nation | Sac & Fox Tribe of the Mississippi in Iowa,https://www.meskwaki.org/,"The Meskwaki Nation is Iowa's only federally recognized Indian tribe. Click to learn about our settlement, find helpful resources, view upcoming events & more.",Meskwaki,Algic
6,"Sharing Meskwaki Ways Through Dance, Music, Beadwork, Foodways",https://artsmidwest.org/stories/sharing-meskwaki-ways-through-dance-music-beadwork-foodways/,"A Meskwaki Mother's Wish Like the mother swan in her dance, Snow is preparing for her youngest to graduate from high school. She fears sending her children off during this era of political upheaval, but tending to tradition helps. Snow is preparing mirrored beadwork that will adorn a harness her son will wear during his graduation ceremony.",Meskwaki,Algic
7,River of Song: Music Along the River - PBS,https://www.pbs.org/riverofsong/music/e1-meskwaki.html,"Most of the Meskwaki lived hidden along the tributaries of the Mississippi until July 13, 185 7, when the first eighty acres were sold to them by a Mr. Isaac Butler along the Iowa River, where the ...",Meskwaki,Algic
8,Meskwaki Nation Singers | Tama IA - Facebook,https://www.facebook.com/people/Meskwaki-Nation-Singers/61550267518807/,"Meskwaki Nation Singers, Tama, IA. 1,305 likes · 11 talking about this. Just here to share some tunes and good vibes!",Meskwaki,Algic
9,Songs and Dances of Great Lake Indians - Smithsonian Folkways Recordings,https://folkways.si.edu/songs-and-dances-of-the-great-lakes-indians/american-indian/music/album/smithsonian,"Gertrude Prokosch Kurath recorded and comments on music performed by the Great Lakes tribes of Algonquin, Meskwaki, Ojibwa, Iroquois and others. On this collection you'll find a fish dance, peace pipe dance and powwow dance; a bear dance, eagle dance and deer song; a medicine song, drinking song and canoe song.",Meskwaki,Algic
